# Documentation maintenance

Whenever you **implement or materially change** behavior (features, routes, validation, API endpoints, DB schema/migrations, env vars, integrations, AI features and agent tools, or user-visible flows), **update documentation in the same change**, not as a follow-up the user must request.

## What to update

| Change type | Update |
| --- | --- |
| Architecture, routes, env vars, API surface, data model | `docs/architecture/*.md`: pick the matching file, add rows/sections |
| Product scope (a feature ships, changes shape, or is descoped) | `docs/prd.md`, kept in sync with what actually ships |
| Page/section behavior, save flows, validation, per-route UX | `docs/guides/routes/*.md` — see `.cursor/rules/route-guides.mdc` |
| Workflow/checkpoint behavior (discovery, tailoring, apply) | `docs/architecture/overview.md` §3 + the owning phase file |
| AI feature or agent tool: new/changed prompt, tier, MCP tool | `docs/architecture/overview.md` + the owning phase file (`docs/phases/phase-12b-*` for MCP tools) |
| Mutating capability (API write, cron, webhook, AI tool write) | `.cursor/rules/audit-logging.mdc` — emit an event or mark N/A |
| Database migration or one-shot backfill instructions | `docs/architecture/deployment.md` § migrations (created in Phase 1/14) |
| Phase task completed / exit criteria met | `docs/phases/<file>.md` checklist + `docs/phases/README.md` status table |
| Global conventions agents rely on | `CLAUDE.md` if the old text would mislead future sessions |

## Rules of thumb

- Prefer **small, accurate edits** over rewriting a whole doc unless the change is cross-cutting.
- If you add a new query param, env var, or HTTP route, document it in the matching `docs/architecture/*.md` table.
- If behavior **diverges** from what a doc says, **fix the doc** — do not leave contradictions.
- Do **not** create extra markdown outside `docs/` and `.cursor/rules/` unless the user asked for it.

## When docs need no change

Trivial fixes (typos, formatting, internal rename with no API/UX impact) do not require doc updates unless they touch documented names.
